      "learned": "Raw data is essentially invisible information: individual numbers or entries listed without organisation reveal very little on their own. A frequency distribution table, built step-by-step using tally marks (gate tallying: IIII), transforms that chaos into a structured summary that shows each data value and how often it occurs (its frequency). Teachers should note: the key conceptual leap here is that organising data does NOT change the data — it only makes the hidden pattern visible.",
